    "created_at": "2021-12-03T11:53:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-03T11:53:45Z",
    "body": "The main reason we safelist response headers is because they could contain confidential information and the variety of teams working on an application might overlook this.\r\n\r\nIf we always expose `Vary` this could lead to exposure of confidential request header names. This seems quite minor, but making changes to the same-origin policy is always tricky. Is `Vary` very important in practice for the Cache API?",
