    "updated_at": "2021-12-03T16:23:18Z",
    "body": "Well, I was trying to align chromium to the cache API spec where we are not supposed to look at the internal response for the vary header.  Switching to ignore vary headers seemed low risk for opaque responses, but seems more risky for CORS responses.  I'm unsure if I'll be able to align there or not.  It would simplify some things (and match my original expectations) if vary was cors safelisted.",
